.\" Tavletta manual page (roff, man(7)); installed by the Debian and RPM packages.
.\" The full documentation: https://tavletta.joshuahirsig.xyz/ and docs/cli.md.
.TH TAVLETTA 1 2026-11-17 "Tavletta 1.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
tavletta \- design and print labels on label printers
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tavletta
.RI [ FILE ...]
.br
.B tavletta print
.I FILE
.RB [ \-\-printer
.IR ID ]
.RB [ \-\-host
.IR ADDR ]
.RB [ \-\-copies
.IR N ]
.RB [ \-\-set
.IR NAME = VALUE ]
.RB [ \-\-data
.IR FILE ]
.RB [ \-\-dry\-run
.RB [ \-\-output
.IR PNG ]]
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B tavletta list\-printers
.RB [ \-\-printer
.IR ID ]
.br
.B tavletta serve
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B tavletta mcp
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B tavletta token new
.I NAME
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B tavletta
.BR \-\-version " | " \-\-help
.SH DESCRIPTION
Tavletta designs labels with text, images, symbols and codes, shows them
exactly as they will be printed and prints them over the network or USB:
on label printers with endless tape or die\-cut labels, and on office
printers, one label per page or on label sheets.
.PP
Without a command the application window opens; label files
.RI ( .tavletta )
given on the command line open in it.
The commands below need no display.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BI print " FILE"
Print a label file without opening a window.
Without
.B \-\-host
the printer set in the application is used, or the only one found.
.RS
.TP
.BI \-\-printer " ID"
printer model, by default the label's:
vc500w, ptouch, brother_ql, brother_ql_diecut, cab, system, dymo, escpos,
niimbot, tspl, epl, zpl
.TP
.BI \-\-host " ADDR"
printer address (host name, IP address or USB device)
.TP
.BI \-\-copies " N"
number of copies
.TP
.BI \-\-set " NAME=VALUE"
text of the element
.IR NAME ,
or value of the variable
.BI {= NAME };
repeatable.
.B \-\-set\-literal
takes the value as it is.
.TP
.BI \-\-counter\-start " N"
counter of the first label
.TP
.B \-\-no\-save\-counter
do not save the next counter value in the label file
.TP
.B \-\-no\-query
do not ask the printer before rendering
.TP
.B \-\-printer\-defaults
print with the printer model's defaults instead of the choices last made
in the application
.TP
.BR \-\-print\-method " printer|transfer|direct"
print method of a thermal printer that has the setting
.TP
.BI \-\-data " FILE"
serial labels: one label for each row of a CSV, ODS or XLSX file;
.BI \-\-sheet " NAME"
and
.BI \-\-rows " FROM\-TO"
choose which
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
check and render only, do not print
.TP
.BI \-\-output " PNG"
with
.BR \-\-dry\-run :
save each label as PNG
.RB ( \-
for standard output: the first only)
.RE
.TP
.B list\-printers
List the printers found on the network: model, address, name.
.TP
.B serve
Run a print server with a REST API and, with
.BR \-\-mcp ,
MCP for AI clients.
It listens on 127.0.0.1:8790 unless
.B \-\-host
and
.B \-\-port
say otherwise.
See
.B tavletta serve \-\-help
for its options.
.TP
.B mcp
Serve MCP on standard input and output, for AI clients.
.TP
.BI "token new" " NAME"
Make an access token for the print server and add its hash to
.IR tokens.toml .
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
printed
.TP
.B 1
printer problem, or no printer found
.TP
.B 2
wrong arguments
.TP
.B 3
the label file cannot be read (or is still locked after 60 s), or the
output not written
.TP
.B 4
the label cannot be printed as it is (empty, unknown variable or column,
a code that cannot be made)
.TP
.B 5
the counter cannot be saved
.TP
.B 130
interrupted (Ctrl+C, SIGTERM or SIGHUP)
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/tavletta/
settings: printers, last choices
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/tavletta/templates/
saved templates
.TP
.I ~/.config/tavletta/tokens.toml
the print server's access tokens
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/tavletta/labels/
the label files the print server uses
.SH SEE ALSO
The user guide: <https://tavletta.joshuahirsig.xyz/>
.br
The command line in detail:
<https://git.joshuahirsig.xyz/joshii/tavletta/src/branch/main/docs/cli.md>
